# Diagnose marker — fix/andon-scan-path-check-plus-per-file-allowlist
- date: 2026-08-31
- branch: fix/andon-scan-path-check-plus-per-file-allowlist
- full /diagnose ceremony landed in prior turn (this session):

## Step 0 — Repro
`gh workflow run publish.yml -f tag=v0.1.0` (run 33346136435) →
checks fail at `Andon scan for operator-private terms` step.
14 hits (12 docs/operator-private/ mentions in prose + 2 emails).
Reproducible 100%. Local `npm publish --dry-run --provenance
--ignore-scripts` after `node scripts/prepublish-bundle-substrate.mjs`
reproduces same 14 hits.

## Step 1 — Is / Is Not
- IS: fires on descriptive prose in substrate/**/*.md files bundled
  from public bassclef; fires on public contact emails in
  substrate/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md + substrate/.claude/skills/promote/SKILL.md
- IS NOT: does not fire on actual private content (no
  substrate/docs/operator-private/ files exist per jq on
  ~/src/sunj-labs/bassclef/lite-manifest.json); does not fire on
  bassclef-cli's own src/ or docs/

## Step 2 — Five Whys
1. Why fail? Scan found 14 hits.
2. Why hits? Public bassclef ships ADRs + skills + docs describing
   operator-private discipline; strings appear in prose.
3. Why does the scan flag prose? Regex matches string anywhere in
   content, no discrimination between path-as-file vs path-as-reference.
4. Why no discrimination? Scan design predates scope-b1 (which added
   substrate/ as new artifact class); scan wasn't updated for the
   new class.
5. Why not updated? Same defect class as #40 — scan integration miss
   when a new artifact class landed.

## Step 3 — Hypothesis
Moving docs/operator-private/ from content-scan to path-scan +
adding per-file allowlist for two public-contact emails cures both
the false-positive class + the sister email false-positive class.

Falsification test: after code lands, run
`npm pack --dry-run --json` on repo with substrate/ populated + run
andon-scan.mjs on it. Should exit 0. Verified locally before push.

## Root cause class
Workflow-integration defect — scan design didn't anticipate
substrate/ as a new artifact class shipped by scope-b1.
